    "calculations": [
      "Use the three fixed 8-position replacement samples verbatim from the source.",
      "Multiplicity is the count of each ID in the revealed sample; extra copies = sample positions − unique IDs.",
      "Out-of-bag is the original row bank minus IDs in the complete sample; an unfinished prefix is not labelled a complete OOB result.",
      "Root candidate thresholds are midpoints of adjacent distinct values in the sampled rows. Weighted Gini uses multiplicities, not just unique rows.",
      "The source fitted root also depends on the declared node feature draw. Inspecting another feature does not rewrite the supplied tree."
    ],
